# SDK design framing

> **Temporary development section.** These pages are the working notes that shaped Karbone, published as-is for the internal
> review. They will be removed or rewritten before the public release; the reference is the code and the guides.


Goal: complete, idiomatic Kotlin client for Carbone API v5 (cloud and on-premise), fixing the gaps of carbone-sdk-java.

## Primary use case

iperia-back (see IPERIA-USAGE.md): self-hosted Community edition, JWT auth optional, docx → PDF/A-3, three operations (upload/render/delete), `data` is an arbitrary object serialized by the app. The SDK must serve this on-premise scenario first-class, cloud second.

## Principles

1. **Immutable per-instance configuration**: `Karbone(apiKey, baseUrl, apiVersion, timeouts, ...)`. No global state. DI-friendly (plain constructor + builder for Java).
2. **Coroutines first**: all I/O methods are `suspend` and `Raise`-based. A thin blocking, throwing facade (`KarboneBlocking` / `.blocking()`) for Java and non-coroutine callers.
3. **Typed request models**: `RenderOptions` data class + DSL builder mirroring the spec 1:1 (`convertTo` as sealed `OutputFormat` with typed `PdfOptions`, `ImageOptions`, `CsvOptions`). `data` accepted as `JsonElement`, `@Serializable` object (with the caller's `Json`/serializer), or a raw JSON string — the raw-string path is required so Jackson-based apps (iperia) can keep their serializer.
4. **Typed errors with Arrow**: `sealed interface KarboneError` (values): `Unauthorized`, `TemplateNotFound`, `RenderNotFound`, `PayloadTooLarge`, `UnsupportedFormat`, `InvalidRequest`, `RenderFailed`, `Transport(cause)`, `Serialization`; API errors carry `status` and the raw `error` text. Primary API is `context(_: Raise<KarboneError>) suspend fun`; `Either` via `either { }`. Java facade `KarboneBlocking` throws `KarboneException(error)`. Request invariants enforced with `ensure` → `InvalidRequest`.
5. **Uniform template input**: `TemplateSource` sealed type — `Path`, `Bytes`, `InputStream/ByteReadChannel`, `Id(String)`. Local SHA-256 computed for Bytes/Path so the hash-first / upload-on-404 flow works fully in memory.
6. **`carbone-version`**: sent by default (5) when targeting the cloud, nullable/omitted for on-premise where the header does not apply. Configurable per client, overridable per call.
7. **Lean dependency footprint**: JDK HttpClient, kotlinx.serialization, arrow-core (`api`), kotlinx-coroutines. Nothing else.

## Proposed surface (package `com.ekino.oss.karbone`)

```kotlin
val karbone = Karbone("api-key") { apiVersion = 5; baseUrl = "https://api.carbone.io"; timeout = 60.seconds }

// Templates
karbone.templates.upload(TemplateSource.path(p), UploadOptions(name = "invoice", versioning = true)): UploadedTemplate
karbone.templates.get(id): ByteArray / stream
karbone.templates.update(id, TemplateMetadataPatch(...))
karbone.templates.delete(id)
karbone.templates.list(ListTemplatesQuery(...)): Page<TemplateSummary>   // + Flow<TemplateSummary> paginating on cursor
karbone.templates.categories(); karbone.templates.tags()

// Rendering
karbone.render(templateId, data) { convertTo = Pdf { watermark("CONFIDENTIAL") }; lang = "fr-fr" }: RenderedDocument(content, filename, contentType)
karbone.render(TemplateSource.bytes(b), data) { ... }          // hash-first, upload on 404, retry
karbone.renderAsync(templateId, data, webhook = Webhook(url, headers)) : RenderStarted
karbone.startRender(templateId, data) { ... }: RenderId         // download=false
karbone.download(renderId): RenderedDocument
karbone.convert(TemplateSource.bytes(docx), to = OutputFormat.Pdf)   // /render/template with no data

// Status
karbone.status(): ApiStatus(version, message)
```

## Decided (see DECISIONS.md)

- HTTP: `java.net.http.HttpClient` behind internal `HttpTransport`. Serialization: kotlinx.serialization.

## Decisions still open

- **Blocking facade**: Java-friendly wrapper in the same module vs separate `karbone-blocking` module.
- **Retries**: none by default, opt-in policy on transport errors (Node SDK retries once on connection reset).
- **Module layout**: single module now; split `core` / `ktor` / `spring-boot-starter` only when needed.

## Test support

Ship a `karbone-test` (or `com.ekino.oss.karbone.test` package) with an in-memory `FakeKarbone` implementing the public client interface, so consumers unit-test without mocking internals. Integration tests of Karbone itself run against `carbone/carbone-ee:full-<version>-fonts` via Testcontainers (Community features, `CARBONE_AUTHENTICATION` on and off).

## Concrete surface

See PUBLIC-API.kt.md (draft v1) for the Kotlin signatures, models, errors and Java facade.
